<p>Everything about this tale was poigniant and topical. I really connected with the writer. The only, ONLY thing that prevents me from upvoting this is that the suicide seems to be shoe-horned in to give it that ZOMG tragedy angle.</p>
<p>Personally, I'd like this more if it was perhaps an open letter to the ethics committee along with a request for resignation and administration of Class-C Amnesiacs.</p>
<p>The idea that this guy would rather off himself instead of going AWOL or asking to resign is odd. Considering the average intelligence of your typical foundation member, not to mention those that could potentially run across containment chambers even the 05's don't know about.. I doubt people with that kind of access or brains would be killing themselves so easily.</p>
<p>Again, otherwise this is a great tale. I really enjoyed it. Nice work, Gargus.</p>

							</div>

								
					
